  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCC- CSO in the digital domain</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cooperation Committee for Cambodia (CCC) is a leading membership based organization for NGOs in Cambodia with nearly 180 members working on various development sector. CCC has been playing roles as the Governance Champion, Coordinator and Advocate torealize enabling environment for CSO and sustained CSO Resource Hub at the national and sub-national levels. Under ReCIPE project, CCC is oneof the implementing partners is working with national networks and think tanks focusing on digital advocacy and policy issues that engage government ministries, academia, private sector and civil society.

Within this project CCC focuses on the following:
1. Strengthen capacity of CSOs on topics related to digital rights through co-creating &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; rolling out in-person &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; virtual training
2. Support the critical analysis of government policy and private sector in the contexts in which the consortium members work to help define and categories the digital rights issues affecting civil society, especially with potentially transformational technology such as Artificial Intelligence.
3. Facilitate national networks of CSOs &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; digital defenders for knowledge sharing and collaborative research and formulation of policy positions, including that related to emerging tech suchas AI.
4. Facilitate round-tablesand forums connecting CSOs and human rights defenders with decision-makers (governments, tech companies etc) in digital arena and
5. Design and implement digital rights awareness raising campaigns.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCC - Cooperation Committee for</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Cooperation Coomiitee for Cambodia (CCC) was established in 1990 as an association of Civil Society Organisations in Cambodia. It is a leading network strengthening the cooperation, professionalism, accountability, governance and effectiveness of itsmembers and representing the sector to the government and donors. It aims to contribute to a cohesive, accountable and transparent NGO sector, contributing more effectively to the development of Cambodia.</narrative>
